  "notes": "Source: official UVU Computer Science department 'COMPUTER SCIENCE - COMPUTER SCIENCE (2026-2027)' recommended sequence flowchart, https://www.uvu.edu/cs/docs/computer-science/cs-cs.pdf — the department's published term-by-term plan for the Computer Science track of the B.S. in Computer Science (catalog year 2026-2027, current). The current catalog program page (catalog.uvu.edu/engineering-technology/computer-science/computer-science-bs/, 'Computer Science, B.S.') publishes no term-by-term sequence, so the department flowchart is the authoritative official sequence. Per the department program page (uvu.edu/cs/computer-science), as of Fall 2026 prior emphases were converted to tracks (Computer Science, Full Stack Web Design, Secure Programming, Artificial Intelligence); this plan is the Computer Science track. Transcription: PDF fetched 2026-09-30; cells extracted with pdftotext -layout and every course/credit verified against 220-DPI renderings of the chart. Chart term totals (16/16/15/14/15/15/15/15) sum to 121 while the department states 120 credits minimum to graduate; total_credits=121 per the chart's own arithmetic. Prerequisite arrows traced visually from the flowchart; only unambiguous arrows encoded (CS 3060 takes the red arrow fed by CS 1380, CS 2420 and CS 2810; CS 3450 and CS 4470 take the choice slot CS 3250/3260/3270/3370/3380 via its slot code). 'See WT' = see Wolverine Track (UVU degree audit); electives are advisor-approved. Starred courses require University Advanced Standing (UAS). Matriculation before 3000/4000-level CS (except CS 3050): (CS 1400 and CS 1410) or CS 1420; CS 2300 and CS 2420 with C+ or higher; MATH 1210 and ENGL 1010 with C or higher; each class max 2 attempts; 2.5 cumulative GPA. Math placement: CS 1400 requires math through high-school algebra & trigonometry; CS 1410 and CS 1380 require math through college algebra (placement guidance, not course prerequisites). Alternate entry: CS 1420 (by entrance exam in SE 407) plus 1 CS elective may substitute for CS 1400 + CS 1410. 'PPCG (See WT)' transcribed verbatim as printed on the chart (a general-education distribution slot; specific course via Wolverine Track). CS 4380 chart text 'Advanced/High Performance C Architecture' rendered with the full official catalog course title 'Advanced High Performance Computer Architecture'.",
